# =========================================================
#  CREDENTIALS - never committed, no exceptions
# =========================================================
# The Google service-account key for reading Drive photo uploads. It lives
# OUTSIDE the repo (~/perimity-secrets/) and is mounted into the container, so
# these patterns should never match anything. They exist because a key that
# gets copied "just for a minute" into the project folder is exactly how one
# ends up in a public repository, and a leaked service-account key cannot be
# rotated by changing a password - it has to be revoked in Cloud Console.
google-drive.json
*service-account*.json
*-credentials.json
secrets/
perimity-secrets/

# Scratch image written by check-profile-verification.sh. It lives beside the
# script rather than in /tmp because Git Bash's curl is a Windows binary and
# cannot open a POSIX /tmp path. Removed on exit, but ignored so an interrupted
# run cannot leave it staged.
perimity-test-photo.*.png

# Excel lock files. Created whenever a spreadsheet is open and deleted when it
# closes - one got committed already, because `git add -A` while a sheet was
# open picks them up and the name is odd enough not to notice in a file list.
~$*

